## Why This Is Asked

Assesses the ability to govern cross-protocol contracts from a single canonical spec, with pragmatic migration, testing, and observability strategies suitable for large-scale API platforms.

## Key Concepts

- **Single source of truth**: An OpenAPI contract drives REST, GraphQL, and gRPC adapters
- **Runtime version negotiation**: Per-tenant deprecation policies enforced by adapters
- **Versioned migration registry**: Tracks schema evolution with contract tests
- **Observability**: Per-tenant tracing and metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Mapping from OpenAPI spec to protocol adapters
function mapOpenApiToRest(openApiSpec, config) {
  return restAdapter.map(config, openApiSpec);
}

function mapOpenApiToGraphQL(openApiSpec, config) {
  return graphqlAdapter.map(config, openApiSpec);
}

function mapOpenApiToGrpc(openApiSpec, config) {
  return grpcAdapter.map(config, openApiSpec);
}
```

