## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical OAuth2 debugging skills, understanding of token lifecycle, and real-world troubleshooting abilities that backend engineers face daily.

## Expected Answer
Strong candidates identify: 1) Refresh token expired/revoked, 2) Scope mismatch between access and refresh tokens, 3) Client configuration issues. They should mention checking token introspection endpoint, reviewing logs, and testing with Postman/curl.

## Code Example
```typescript
// Debug refresh token failure
async function debugRefreshToken(refreshToken: string) {
  try {
    // 1. Check token introspection
    const introspect = await fetch('/oauth/introspect', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: `token=${refreshToken}`
    });

    // 2. Validate client configuration
    const clientConfig = await getClientConfig();

    // 3. Review token storage
    const storedToken = await getStoredToken(refreshToken);

    return { introspect, clientConfig, storedToken };
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Debug failed:', error);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of cross-service orchestration, eventual consistency, and fault handling in microservices that use event sourcing and CQRS. It also probes patterns like outbox, idempotency, and compensating actions.

## Key Concepts
- Saga orchestration across multiple bounded contexts
- Event contracts and versioning for backward compatibility
- Outbox pattern for at-least-once delivery and durability
- Idempotent handlers keyed by correlationId
- Compensation actions to maintain consistency

## Code Example
```typescript
type Event = { type: string; payload: any; correlationId: string };
type Command = { type: string; payload: any; correlationId: string };

function handleEvent(e: Event) {
  const { type, payload, correlationId } = e;
  switch (type) {
    case 'CartCheckedOut':
      enqueue({ type: 'InventoryReserve', payload, correlationId });
      break;
    case 'InventoryReserved':
      enqueue({ type: 'PaymentCharge', payload, correlationId });
      break;
    case 'PaymentApproved':
      enqueue({ type: 'FinalizeOrder', payload, correlationId });
      break;
    case 'PaymentDeclined':
    case 'InventoryReserveFailed':
      enqueue({ type: 'CancelOrder', payload, correlationId });
      break;
  }
  // simple dedupe check
  if (alreadyProcessed(correlationId, type)) return;
  markProcessed(correlationId, type);
}
``` 

